{"id":948,"date":"2018-11-28T19:52:42","date_gmt":"2018-11-28T19:52:42","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?p=948"},"modified":"2021-06-10T12:42:40","modified_gmt":"2021-06-10T12:42:40","slug":"aims-ghana-remembers-prof-francis-k-a-allotey","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/aims-ghana-remembers-prof-francis-k-a-allotey\/","title":{"rendered":"AIMS GHANA REMEMBERS PROF. FRANCIS K. A. ALLOTEY"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>AIMS GHANA organised a Memorial Service in honour of the Late Prof. Francis K. A. Allotey, former President of AIMS Ghana and Founding Trustee of AIMS-NEI, who passed on a year ago.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Led by the Catholic Priest of Cape Coast, Fr. Anthony Hayford, AIMS Ghana community had a Mass in honour of the fallen legend. The priest encouraged the community to learn from Prof. Allotey\u2019s humility and dedication to his work.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Islamic prayers were led by the Imam of Makessim, Issa Adam for the departed soul and AIMS. Present at the memorial service were the Chief Operating Officer, Mr. Moulaye Camara, Prof. Francis Benyah (University of Cape Coast), Prof. Babatude Onasanya (University of Ibadan), Staff, Researchers, Students, Tutors and Service Providers.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>AIMS GHANA organised a Memorial Service in honour of the Late Prof. Francis K. A. Allotey, former President of AIMS Ghana and Founding Trustee of AIMS-NEI, who passed on a year ago. Led by the Catholic Priest of Cape Coast, Fr. Anthony Hayford, AIMS Ghana community had a Mass in honour of the fallen legend.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":949,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"news_types":[32],"acf":[],"author_meta":{"display_name":"rose","author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/rose\/"},"featured_img"